    <string name="clip_info_title">Which models to use?</string>
    <string name="clip_info_body">You need two model files (an Image Model and a Text Model) in ONNX format (.onnx). Both models must output the same embedding size, and the text model must accept token IDs. Standard CLIP ViT-B/32 models work perfectly.\n\nThe default models used here were:\n- vision_model_quantized.onnx for image\n- text_model_quantized.onnx for text.\n
        \nIt uses the image model to look at every photo in your library and generates a mathematical fingerprint (embedding) for it.
        \nIt then uses the Text Model to translate your search phrase into an embedding, compare it to your photo embeddings, and match your search!
    </string>
    <string name="clip_info_close">Got it</string>
